/*
 * Formatted strings(`f"...${expr}..."`) are desugared into a slice concatenation
 * of their literal parts and a `std::conv::to!{[cX]}(expr)` conversion of each
 * interpolated part, then reparsed and validated like ordinary source code. This
 * lets ordinary constant folding collapse a fully constant format string into a
 * single string constant, without any dedicated compile-time formatting logic.

 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::validator::value::literal::string::format
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/validator/value/literal/string/format.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created (YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-08-23
 * @Copyright (C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
